---
import ContentLayout from "../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { PLATFORM_STYLES } from "../../components/embedGrid/platformStyles";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="How to Watch Multiple Live Streams at Once | Stream Mix"
  description="Learn how to watch multiple Twitch, YouTube, and Kick streams at once in a customizable browser grid with video and chat."
  heading="How to watch multiple live streams at once"
>
  <p>
    Stream Mix places multiple live broadcasts in one browser workspace. You can
    combine <span class={PLATFORM_STYLES.twitch.text}>Twitch</span> channels,
    <span class={PLATFORM_STYLES.youtube.text}>YouTube</span> live streams, and
    <span class={PLATFORM_STYLES.kick.text}>Kick</span> channels, then choose whether
    each window shows its video, chat, or both.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Paste a URL or enter the identifier</h2>
  <p>
    The quickest option is to paste the complete stream URL. Stream Mix detects
    the supported platform and extracts the identifier automatically.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      For <span class={PLATFORM_STYLES.twitch.text}>Twitch</span>, paste
      <code>https://twitch.tv/channel</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      For <span class={PLATFORM_STYLES.youtube.text}>YouTube</span>, paste
      <code>https://youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID</code> or
      <code>https://youtu.be/VIDEO_ID</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      For <span class={PLATFORM_STYLES.kick.text}>Kick</span>, paste
      <code>https://kick.com/channel</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you prefer, select the platform manually and enter only the Twitch or
    Kick channel name, or the YouTube video ID.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Add the stream</h2>
  <p>
    Open <a href="/">Stream Mix</a> and paste the URL. The platform selector updates
    automatically. Then choose Stream + Chat, Stream, or Chat and select Add to create
    a new window. You can still select a platform and enter its identifier manually.
    Repeat the process for every perspective you want to follow.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Arrange the grid</h2>
  <p>
    Drag a window using its title bar and resize it from either lower corner.
    Make the primary broadcast larger and keep secondary perspectives or chats
    nearby. Window positions are saved automatically in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Reclaim viewing space</h2>
  <p>
    Enable Compact mode to hide the site header and let video and chat use more
    of the workspace. Move the pointer to the top edge of a window whenever you
    need its drag, close, minimize, or fullscreen controls.
  </p>

  <h2>Common multistream use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Follow several players’ perspectives during an esports tournament.</li>
    <li>Watch an official broadcast alongside creator co-streams.</li>
    <li>Monitor live coverage occurring on more than one platform.</li>
    <li>Keep a main video large while following one or more chats.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Playback considerations</h2>
  <p>
    Every additional stream uses bandwidth and processing power. If playback
    stutters, reduce the quality inside secondary players, show chat without
    video where appropriate, or close streams you are not actively watching.
    Streams may also have slightly different broadcast delays because each
    platform delivers its own player independently.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Watch multiple streams</a></p>
</ContentLayout>
